1
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:42,960
It'll work out somehow, right?

2
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:47,200
Wahahahahaha!

3
00:00:56,040 --> 00:00:59,900
Anyone without work, come to me.

4
00:01:00,560 --> 00:01:04,520
I don't have any either, but don't worry.

5
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:18,260
Look, Akaneru's burning too.
It'll work out eventually.

6
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:27,460
You understand, right? Got it, got it.
Once you get it, just shut up and follow me.

7
00:01:40,860 --> 00:01:43,600
Sagaren BV, Master Kāhikichi.

8
00:01:49,540 --> 00:01:52,000
What are you planning to
do with a doll like that?

9
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:55,240
We're holding a traffic safety class at the elementary school today,
remember?

10
00:01:55,740 --> 00:01:58,840
This doll is going to play the part
of the person getting hit by the car.

11
00:01:58,840 --> 00:02:02,380
Even if it's just a papier-mâché truck,
we can't risk anyone getting hurt.

12
00:02:02,380 --> 00:02:04,200
I see, alright, let me take a look.

13
00:02:04,520 --> 00:02:06,980
No, not yet! You haven't made any progress!

14
00:02:07,140 --> 00:02:08,620
Alright! It's fine, it's fine!

15
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:10,480
Like this...

16
00:02:12,080 --> 00:02:13,180
It looks just like him!

17
00:02:13,220 --> 00:02:14,920
Like this, and like this, and like this!

18
00:02:15,060 --> 00:02:18,080
When I imagine this guy getting hit...

19
00:02:20,540 --> 00:02:22,300
Give it back already, Ryo-chan!

20
00:02:22,440 --> 00:02:23,760
Not yet, not yet!

21
00:02:23,880 --> 00:02:25,100
Just give it back!

22
00:02:25,320 --> 00:02:25,580
Yes!

23
00:02:26,040 --> 00:02:31,360
The Chief's head...

24
00:02:31,360 --> 00:02:33,420
Chief!

25
00:02:34,520 --> 00:02:36,360
What's wrong with my head?

26
00:02:36,520 --> 00:02:38,180
Well nothing.

27
00:02:38,180 --> 00:02:40,120
You idiot!

28
00:02:40,120 --> 00:02:40,720
Shoo!

29
00:02:41,020 --> 00:02:41,744
Ryotsu,

30
00:02:41,794 --> 00:02:45,200
you'll be the one making a
replacement for the broken dummy.

31
00:02:45,200 --> 00:02:46,620
Me? Wh-what?

32
00:02:47,040 --> 00:02:48,155
Listen, everyone.

33
00:02:48,205 --> 00:02:51,700
Today, principals from elementary schools
across the area will be coming to observe.

34
00:02:52,180 --> 00:02:54,900
Make sure your instruction is
something we can be proud of.

35
00:02:55,460 --> 00:02:55,860
Yes!

36
00:02:56,160 --> 00:02:58,860
Um, mm

37
00:03:12,120 --> 00:03:15,640
At intersections,
even if the pedestrian signal is green,

38
00:03:15,640 --> 00:03:17,540
if you suddenly dash out,

39
00:03:18,100 --> 00:03:19,600
La-la-la-laan!

40
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:22,560
cars rushing toward you out of nowhere

41
00:03:23,880 --> 00:03:24,860
Drag!

42
00:03:24,860 --> 00:03:26,080
Drag!

43
00:03:26,080 --> 00:03:28,180
that's what happens, so let's be careful.

44
00:03:28,180 --> 00:03:29,400
Yes!

45
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:31,560
Ryo-san, are you all right?

46
00:03:31,560 --> 00:03:33,660
Be gentler about it!

47
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:36,340
Nakagawa, I can't hold on.

48
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:41,700
No, it's nothing. Never mind.

49
00:03:42,060 --> 00:03:45,404
At pedestrian crossings,
even when the light turns green,

50
00:03:45,454 --> 00:03:48,340
always look both ways before crossing.

51
00:03:48,640 --> 00:03:49,320
Okay!

52
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:53,460
Just because few cars pass by,
playing in the road,

53
00:03:53,520 --> 00:03:57,400
you may not be visible to cars backing up.

54
00:03:57,600 --> 00:03:58,280
Really?

55
00:03:58,680 --> 00:04:01,220
So, let's be careful so this doesn't happen.

56
00:04:01,840 --> 00:04:02,640
Okay!

57
00:04:04,780 --> 00:04:08,700
Geez, I'd hate to get knocked
down over and over again.

58
00:04:08,700 --> 00:04:09,720
That hurts!

59
00:04:10,620 --> 00:04:11,720
Ow

60
00:04:11,720 --> 00:04:13,600
My canned coffee!

61
00:04:14,800 --> 00:04:16,370
What -

62
00:04:16,420 --> 00:04:19,660
What on earth happened?

63
00:04:19,660 --> 00:04:20,920
It's a chimpanzee.

64
00:04:23,220 --> 00:04:24,380
Listen, Miotsu.

65
00:04:24,380 --> 00:04:26,160
I know, this guy -

66
00:04:29,120 --> 00:04:30,580
Are you all right? Are you hurt?

67
00:04:30,580 --> 00:04:33,020
Yes, but my handbag...

68
00:04:34,740 --> 00:04:36,460
We have to catch that chimpanzee.

69
00:04:36,460 --> 00:04:37,300
Yes, yes.

70
00:04:37,840 --> 00:04:39,440
Give back that handbag!

71
00:04:43,900 --> 00:04:46,080
How dare that idiot mock us!

72
00:04:48,660 --> 00:04:50,400
Don't let him get away, Ryotsu!

73
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:51,840
Hang in there, Ryo-chan!

74
00:04:51,840 --> 00:04:53,480
You can do it, Ryo-san!

75
00:04:54,120 --> 00:04:54,960
Alright!

76
00:04:54,960 --> 00:04:56,580
That's right!

77
00:04:57,840 --> 00:04:59,020
We've got him!

78
00:05:00,960 --> 00:05:01,720
He fell!

79
00:05:01,720 --> 00:05:03,400
Let's go check it out, Chief.

80
00:05:03,400 --> 00:05:03,780
Okay.

81
00:05:06,760 --> 00:05:10,040
If you hand it back quietly,
I'll trade you a banana for it.

82
00:05:12,100 --> 00:05:13,480
That's right. Got it?

83
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:16,760
Good, good. As long as you understand.

84
00:05:16,760 --> 00:05:19,260
We got the handbag back.

85
00:05:19,800 --> 00:05:22,980
Wow, you actually talked
a chimpanzee into it!

86
00:05:22,980 --> 00:05:24,800
Only Ryo-chan could pull that off.

87
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:27,380
He's closer to a chimpanzee than to a human.

88
00:05:29,940 --> 00:05:31,360
Be careful on the way.

89
00:05:31,360 --> 00:05:35,900
Well, well. The chimp being transported to the zoo escaped,
of all things.

90
00:05:35,900 --> 00:05:39,380
You never know what's going
to happen in this world.

91
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:40,720
That's wonderful!

92
00:05:40,720 --> 00:05:43,860
He's exactly the talent
I've been searching for.

93
00:05:45,500 --> 00:05:47,300
What, me as a teacher?

94
00:05:48,080 --> 00:05:50,860
Yes, we already have the
station chief's approval.

95
00:05:50,860 --> 00:05:52,060
Really?

96
00:05:52,060 --> 00:05:53,840
Or rather, are you serious?

97
00:05:53,840 --> 00:05:58,580
If you make a man like this a teacher,
the students will end up copying his idiocy.

98
00:05:58,580 --> 00:06:00,640
Chief, you can't be serious!

99
00:06:01,360 --> 00:06:04,260
Anyway, Ryo-chan,
do you even have a teaching certificate?

100
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:06,480
As if I'd have something like that!

101
00:06:07,080 --> 00:06:10,080
Being a teacher doesn't mean
teaching studies, though.

102
00:06:10,080 --> 00:06:12,040
Your wild, rugged strength,

103
00:06:12,040 --> 00:06:16,020
and your expressive way of talking with chimpanzees
as if they were friends for a hundred years.

104
00:06:16,700 --> 00:06:19,820
That's exactly what we'd love
our students to learn from you.

105
00:06:20,260 --> 00:06:22,260
I don't mean that you should teach them,
exactly.

106
00:06:22,260 --> 00:06:25,560
Just show the students who you really are.

107
00:06:26,120 --> 00:06:29,100
But, well, I'm not the teacher type, am I?

108
00:06:29,100 --> 00:06:32,320
Our school needs someone like you.

109
00:06:32,320 --> 00:06:33,400
Well, but...

110
00:06:33,800 --> 00:06:35,600
Of course, we'll give you a reward.

111
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:37,020
A reward? What kind?

112
00:06:38,060 --> 00:06:41,220
You've got a good eye,
choosing me as a teacher.

113
00:06:41,220 --> 00:06:45,600
I was born to guide people, you know.

114
00:06:45,600 --> 00:06:47,780
How convenient for you.

115
00:06:47,780 --> 00:06:49,980
Mention money and he's all in

116
00:06:49,980 --> 00:06:53,220
Fine, I'll take the job for
the sake of Japan's future.

117
00:06:53,220 --> 00:06:54,680
So where is it, exactly?

118
00:06:56,100 --> 00:06:58,240
Technically, it's in Tokyo.

119
00:06:59,100 --> 00:07:01,115
Here it is. Shōdō Island?

120
00:07:01,165 --> 00:07:03,460
The one from "Twenty-Four Eyes"?

121
00:07:03,920 --> 00:07:06,340
No, but the location's different, isn't it?

122
00:07:06,340 --> 00:07:08,480
Shōdō Island is in the Seto Inland Sea,
after all.

123
00:07:08,480 --> 00:07:12,540
Around here, we call our island
"Azuki Island."

124
00:07:12,540 --> 00:07:13,740
Azuki Island?

125
00:07:28,600 --> 00:07:30,160
That's Shodoshima over there.

126
00:07:30,160 --> 00:07:33,240
It really is a tiny island,
like a grain of bean.

127
00:07:33,240 --> 00:07:33,758
Yes,

128
00:07:33,808 --> 00:07:37,600
but it's full of nature
and a wonderful island.

129
00:07:44,840 --> 00:07:46,040
Here we are.

130
00:07:51,660 --> 00:07:55,240
For sleeping, you can use the duty room,
so please make use of it.

131
00:07:56,400 --> 00:07:59,100
This is Ryotsu-sensei's classroom.

132
00:07:59,720 --> 00:08:02,020
Just the third grade has two classes?

133
00:08:02,020 --> 00:08:04,900
For such a small island,
there sure are a lot of students.

134
00:08:04,900 --> 00:08:08,980
No, from first to sixth grade
there's only one class each.

135
00:08:08,980 --> 00:08:10,780
Then what's this?

136
00:08:10,780 --> 00:08:10,980
This one?

137
00:08:11,080 --> 00:08:13,660
I like him, the blond teacher.

138
00:08:14,680 --> 00:08:17,075
For the next week, starting today,
as a special teacher,

139
00:08:17,125 --> 00:08:20,640
Ryotsu-sensei will be
looking after all of you.

140
00:08:20,900 --> 00:08:23,962
Everyone,
listen carefully to what Ryotsu-sensei says,

141
00:08:24,012 --> 00:08:25,940
and study hard, okay?

142
00:08:26,760 --> 00:08:30,460
One, two, three, four... twelve kids in all

143
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:31,580
Teacher Ryotsu.

144
00:08:32,460 --> 00:08:35,000
Well, I'll leave them to you,
Teacher Ryotsu.

145
00:08:35,360 --> 00:08:36,889
But I'm only just now wondering,

146
00:08:36,939 --> 00:08:39,380
what exactly am I supposed to do?

147
00:08:40,780 --> 00:08:41,820
Please play with them.

148
00:08:42,360 --> 00:08:43,060
Play?

149
00:08:43,160 --> 00:08:45,580
Yes, I'm counting on you.

150
00:08:48,700 --> 00:08:51,180
Why do I have to play with these brats?

151
00:08:51,180 --> 00:08:53,820
Still, there's the reward, so...

152
00:08:54,300 --> 00:08:56,540
Yes, then first, a self-introduction.

153
00:08:57,300 --> 00:08:58,760
Sara-sara-sara...

154
00:09:00,860 --> 00:09:03,140
Hey, everyone, I'm Ryotsu Kankichi.

155
00:09:03,140 --> 00:09:04,880
Call me Teacher Kankichi.

156
00:09:09,300 --> 00:09:11,000
We can't let them walk all over us here!

157
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,580
First impressions are everything, you know.

158
00:09:13,580 --> 00:09:17,200
In those school dramas on TV, this is when

159
00:09:19,620 --> 00:09:20,580
you say, "Listen up, all of you!"

160
00:09:20,580 --> 00:09:24,060
The character for
"person" is two strokes leaning on each other,

161
00:09:24,060 --> 00:09:24,660
teacher -

162
00:09:25,360 --> 00:09:27,640
Wait, that's not "person," that's "enter."

163
00:09:28,800 --> 00:09:29,920
Oops.

164
00:09:30,480 --> 00:09:32,340
Not that it matters or anything.

165
00:09:34,740 --> 00:09:35,860
Koichi?

166
00:09:36,440 --> 00:09:37,600
What are you up to right now?

167
00:09:37,760 --> 00:09:39,800
What are you talking about?
We're in the middle of class!

168
00:09:43,340 --> 00:09:47,340
What's with these kids,
using their phones in the same classroom

169
00:09:47,340 --> 00:09:47,783
I mean,

170
00:09:47,833 --> 00:09:52,640
first you install it, then download
the upgraded data from the site

171
00:09:52,640 --> 00:09:54,620
That face looks like a gorilla!

172
00:09:55,200 --> 00:09:56,020
Look!

173
00:09:57,020 --> 00:09:58,260
Ahahahaha

174
00:10:00,460 --> 00:10:02,320
It's an island full of nature,

175
00:10:02,320 --> 00:10:05,200
so I thought it'd be all summer vegetables,

176
00:10:05,200 --> 00:10:06,920
but this is just bean
sprouts grown in the shade!

177
00:10:10,500 --> 00:10:11,400
Be quiet!

178
00:10:11,880 --> 00:10:13,580
Stop talking on your phones!

179
00:10:17,280 --> 00:10:19,460
Twelve megs really is a must, after all.

180
00:10:20,020 --> 00:10:20,480
So, anyway,

181
00:10:22,120 --> 00:10:23,860
Listen to what people are saying!

182
00:10:25,540 --> 00:10:28,300
If the person next to you lets their phone ring,
tell them to knock it off.

183
00:10:28,300 --> 00:10:30,100
It gets in the way of studying, you know.

184
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:35,520
What's with this dead atmosphere?

185
00:10:35,900 --> 00:10:40,160
Unlike people in the old days, we're the
type who don't interfere with each other.

186
00:10:40,880 --> 00:10:41,580
What did you say?

187
00:10:42,240 --> 00:10:45,040
So, teacher, just leave us alone.

188
00:10:45,040 --> 00:10:48,560
If we all just do the same thing,
there won't be any fights.

189
00:10:49,120 --> 00:10:52,020
Sweating it out and working
hard is uncool, right?

190
00:10:54,860 --> 00:10:55,600
Times have...

191
00:10:56,140 --> 00:10:58,340
They're making fun of me!

192
00:10:58,340 --> 00:11:01,300
This is nothing like
the school dramas on TV!

193
00:11:01,300 --> 00:11:03,160
No, no, this won't do.

194
00:11:03,160 --> 00:11:04,600
I can't lose my temper here.

195
00:11:04,600 --> 00:11:05,380
Y-yeah, that's it!

196
00:11:05,380 --> 00:11:08,340
Let's get through this with
the classic school-drama sport!

197
00:11:09,220 --> 00:11:11,300
O-okay!

198
00:11:11,300 --> 00:11:13,200
Let's all play soccer!

199
00:11:13,200 --> 00:11:15,140
We can't play soccer!

200
00:11:15,140 --> 00:11:16,600
No way!

201
00:11:16,600 --> 00:11:17,300
Here we go!

202
00:11:19,700 --> 00:11:21,100
Alright, here we go.

203
00:11:22,060 --> 00:11:22,740
Well then.

204
00:11:24,680 --> 00:11:27,100
Oops, did I kick it too hard?

205
00:11:27,100 --> 00:11:30,920
Not that it matters, but if we don't hurry,
it'll roll right into the sea.

206
00:11:30,920 --> 00:11:34,500
There's hardly any flat
ground on this tiny island.

207
00:11:34,500 --> 00:11:35,700
What?

208
00:11:35,700 --> 00:11:40,680
Wait, wait!

209
00:11:42,920 --> 00:11:43,720
Damn it.

210
00:11:44,440 --> 00:11:45,860
Alright, there!

211
00:11:51,660 --> 00:11:52,460
How about that?

212
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:54,480
Got it properly!

213
00:11:55,040 --> 00:11:56,380
I forgot to mention something,

214
00:11:56,380 --> 00:11:59,620
but there are sharks swarming in that sea.

215
00:11:59,620 --> 00:12:01,320
Sharks?

216
00:12:04,460 --> 00:12:06,680
A hot-blooded teacher like this

217
00:12:06,680 --> 00:12:08,600
is actually a nuisance these days, you know.

218
00:12:09,620 --> 00:12:11,080
Help me!

219
00:12:24,380 --> 00:12:25,980
You spoiled brats!

220
00:12:25,980 --> 00:12:28,440
You should show your teacher some respect!

221
00:12:33,720 --> 00:12:35,140
This won't do.

222
00:12:35,140 --> 00:12:37,200
Sorry, I was spacing out.

223
00:12:37,200 --> 00:12:38,100
Sorry.

224
00:12:38,900 --> 00:12:40,440
No, well, I...

225
00:12:40,440 --> 00:12:42,220
You're Kankichi Ryotsu-sensei, right?

226
00:12:42,220 --> 00:12:44,800
The principal has told me about you.

227
00:12:45,440 --> 00:12:47,260
The kind of ringleader kid we used to have

228
00:12:47,260 --> 00:12:49,300
who just grew up into a man like you.

229
00:12:49,700 --> 00:12:50,100
Well...

230
00:12:51,020 --> 00:12:52,640
Sorry for the late greeting.

231
00:12:52,640 --> 00:12:55,320
I'm Hideko Takaishi. Nice to meet you.

232
00:12:56,380 --> 00:12:57,720
Likewise, nice to meet you.

233
00:12:58,640 --> 00:13:01,200
You must be worn out after
your first lesson, right?

234
00:13:02,160 --> 00:13:04,780
Totally. These damn kids these days -

235
00:13:04,780 --> 00:13:08,960
they just have no charm at all.

236
00:13:08,960 --> 00:13:11,120
Not that they're bad kids, though.

237
00:13:11,120 --> 00:13:14,500
Like the principal said,
something's missing.

238
00:13:15,200 --> 00:13:17,600
But I believe in you, Ryotsu-sensei.

239
00:13:17,600 --> 00:13:20,060
Would Kankichi-sensei be better?

240
00:13:20,500 --> 00:13:24,780
I'm sure you'll guide the students
of this school in the right direction.

241
00:13:25,460 --> 00:13:28,200
I think the principal has a good eye.

242
00:13:28,200 --> 00:13:29,760
Takaishi-sensei.

243
00:13:30,820 --> 00:13:32,840
Good luck, Kankichi-sensei.

244
00:13:33,280 --> 00:13:33,960
Y-yes!

245
00:13:34,060 --> 00:13:37,360
Ryotsu, Kankichi,
I will fulfill my mission splendidly.

246
00:13:57,180 --> 00:14:00,820
Do I really have to get
along with those cocky brats?

247
00:14:04,820 --> 00:14:05,960
Hello, Ryotsu speaking.

248
00:14:06,880 --> 00:14:08,760
It's Nakagawa.

249
00:14:09,360 --> 00:14:10,620
Reiko's here too.

250
00:14:10,620 --> 00:14:11,700
Want me to put her on?

251
00:14:11,700 --> 00:14:15,360
So, Ryo-chan, are you doing okay?

252
00:14:15,360 --> 00:14:16,680
So-so.

253
00:14:16,680 --> 00:14:19,240
The chief is really worried about you.

254
00:14:20,600 --> 00:14:28,880
He's worried the kids will all turn out like you, Ryo-chan.
"What's wrong with being like me?"
"Don't take it out on me!"

255
00:14:29,240 --> 00:14:36,940
The chief said so, so when I was a kid...
Wait, that's it! I'll go that route. Put Nakagawa on.

256
00:14:36,940 --> 00:14:38,460
I have a favor to ask you.

257
00:14:49,160 --> 00:14:52,400
Nakagawa actually delivered it already?

258
00:14:58,260 --> 00:15:01,280
Look, the latest model of mobile phone!

259
00:15:01,280 --> 00:15:02,480
What's wrong?

260
00:15:03,080 --> 00:15:04,020
Want it?

261
00:15:08,480 --> 00:15:11,360
I'm not just giving it away.
This is going to be the prize.

262
00:15:11,920 --> 00:15:12,640
Prize?

263
00:15:12,640 --> 00:15:13,680
What are you talking about?

264
00:15:13,680 --> 00:15:17,140
You and I are going to
play survival hide-and-seek.

265
00:15:17,140 --> 00:15:19,420
You can hide anywhere on this island.

266
00:15:19,420 --> 00:15:22,380
Of course,
you can keep in touch by phone too.

267
00:15:22,380 --> 00:15:25,960
If you fail to find
everyone before the sun sets,

268
00:15:25,960 --> 00:15:28,080
I'll quietly return to Tokyo.

269
00:15:28,080 --> 00:15:32,040
The one who's left undiscovered
until the end gets this phone.

270
00:15:32,040 --> 00:15:32,740
What do you say?

271
00:15:34,020 --> 00:15:34,600
And if I lose?

272
00:15:35,040 --> 00:15:36,400
I won't do anything.

273
00:15:36,400 --> 00:15:37,760
Same as always.

274
00:15:37,760 --> 00:15:40,000
See? No loss on your end, right?

275
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:41,620
This is a piece of cake.

276
00:15:42,080 --> 00:15:44,060
Alright, let's all do it!

277
00:15:44,060 --> 00:15:48,180
It's just like when I was a kid.

278
00:15:48,180 --> 00:15:50,640
First, bait them with stuff. Success!

279
00:15:51,120 --> 00:15:51,620
Got it?

280
00:15:51,620 --> 00:15:53,820
After ten minutes,
I'm coming to look for you.

281
00:15:56,960 --> 00:15:58,740
There are more places
to hide in the mountains.

282
00:15:58,740 --> 00:15:59,920
Takaichi's over there.

283
00:15:59,920 --> 00:16:01,060
Norika's that way.

284
00:16:01,440 --> 00:16:01,800
Yeah.

285
00:16:06,440 --> 00:16:13,420
Ryotsu-sensei is finally getting started with something!
Right, ten minutes have passed.

286
00:16:14,680 --> 00:16:17,600
First, the mountains. Here I go!

287
00:16:30,500 --> 00:16:32,420
Over here, spotted Hiro.

288
00:16:34,240 --> 00:16:35,500
Found Hiro.

289
00:16:40,080 --> 00:16:41,560
Hiro's been found.

290
00:16:41,560 --> 00:16:44,180
As proof I found him, I'm taking his phone.

291
00:16:44,180 --> 00:16:46,040
How did you figure it out so quickly?

292
00:16:46,040 --> 00:16:49,540
Put a lookout at the
spot with the best view.

293
00:16:49,540 --> 00:16:50,900
Well, it's common sense.

294
00:16:51,260 --> 00:16:52,180
Now, next...

295
00:16:55,840 --> 00:16:59,280
If they come from where Hiro was, run
toward the water mill hut and you'll be fine.

296
00:16:59,280 --> 00:17:00,640
Let's go.

297
00:17:04,520 --> 00:17:06,140
Daisuke and Tomoko found!

298
00:17:06,720 --> 00:17:08,060
How did you know we were here?

299
00:17:09,840 --> 00:17:13,000
Life doesn't always go by the manual.

300
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:14,960
Now hand over your phones.

301
00:17:15,540 --> 00:17:17,420
Hiding in the watermill is pointless.

302
00:17:17,420 --> 00:17:19,760
I can see everything from here,
so don't even try.

303
00:17:25,860 --> 00:17:27,860
Aaaaaah!

304
00:17:27,860 --> 00:17:29,740
This is bad.

305
00:17:31,340 --> 00:17:32,680
Nori found!

306
00:17:37,360 --> 00:17:38,880
Masahiko and Toshiyo found!

307
00:17:39,440 --> 00:17:40,620
Yayoi found!

308
00:17:43,560 --> 00:17:44,280
Sori.

309
00:17:47,040 --> 00:17:48,460
Yoshiko and Naomi found!

310
00:17:51,920 --> 00:17:53,240
Boy-ji found!

311
00:17:54,240 --> 00:17:57,740
Shin'ichirō found!

312
00:17:58,190 --> 00:17:58,820
dp

313
00:18:05,460 --> 00:18:10,620
Well, well, Takahashi's been caught too.
Looks like it's only a matter of time here, too.

314
00:18:11,320 --> 00:18:12,820
Nooooo!

315
00:18:12,820 --> 00:18:13,840
Aaaaaaah!

316
00:18:18,580 --> 00:18:21,900
Eh... eh...

317
00:18:21,900 --> 00:18:22,980
Whoa!

318
00:18:23,780 --> 00:18:27,395
Hiro's caught, Daisuke,
Tomoko, Noriko, Yoshiko, Naomi,

319
00:18:27,445 --> 00:18:30,840
Koichi, Yayoi, Masahiko,
Shinichiro, Toshio...

320
00:18:30,840 --> 00:18:33,640
One short. Where's Kenta?

321
00:18:33,940 --> 00:18:36,960
Kenta won't be found, no way. He's smart.

322
00:18:37,761 --> 00:18:41,620
Did he avoid the mountain with all
its hiding spots and run off to the sea?

323
00:18:42,020 --> 00:18:42,520
Yeah, yeah.

324
00:18:57,600 --> 00:18:59,740
The tide's coming in, what do we do?

325
00:19:02,680 --> 00:19:05,400
I dropped my phone,
so we can't contact anyone either.

326
00:19:05,400 --> 00:19:07,540
And we can't even get out.

327
00:19:07,540 --> 00:19:10,100
If the water keeps rising to the ceiling...

328
00:19:10,100 --> 00:19:11,900
Somebody help us!

329
00:19:12,720 --> 00:19:14,500
Someone, someone!

330
00:19:16,520 --> 00:19:19,780
Even if we shout here, no one will hear us.

331
00:19:21,320 --> 00:19:25,160
This is strange, searching this
long and still not finding anyone.

332
00:19:25,820 --> 00:19:28,880
Has anyone gotten a message from Kenta?

333
00:19:31,720 --> 00:19:33,260
What happened?

334
00:19:35,360 --> 00:19:37,040
Help, someone!

335
00:19:39,120 --> 00:19:41,300
Did you just hear something?

336
00:19:41,300 --> 00:19:44,240
Nope, nothing, nothing.

337
00:19:45,080 --> 00:19:46,440
Let's listen carefully.

338
00:19:48,820 --> 00:19:50,880
I can only hear the sound of the waves.

339
00:19:50,880 --> 00:19:54,060
No, I definitely heard it, from down below.

340
00:19:55,520 --> 00:19:57,720
There's no place to hide down there.

341
00:19:57,720 --> 00:20:00,400
Be careful, if you fall,
there are loads of sharks.

342
00:20:00,400 --> 00:20:01,580
Be quiet.

343
00:20:05,980 --> 00:20:07,540
It's definitely below here after all.

344
00:20:09,160 --> 00:20:10,960
Found it, that cave!

345
00:20:12,980 --> 00:20:16,380
They were hiding, and the tide
came in and cut off the way out.

346
00:20:16,840 --> 00:20:18,560
But how do we rescue them?

347
00:20:18,560 --> 00:20:22,060
Yeah, the entrance is already underwater.

348
00:20:22,060 --> 00:20:23,780
Okay, bring a rope.

349
00:20:23,780 --> 00:20:26,320
There's no way we can get down there.

350
00:20:26,320 --> 00:20:28,380
If we don't go down,
we can't save them, right?

351
00:20:28,380 --> 00:20:30,340
Move your body more than you would on land.

352
00:20:31,420 --> 00:20:34,020
Hey Kenta, we're coming to save you!

353
00:20:34,980 --> 00:20:37,280
Help, somebody, hurry!

354
00:20:38,040 --> 00:20:40,320
Listen, this rope is your lifeline.

355
00:20:41,300 --> 00:20:42,840
Hold on tight and don't let go!

356
00:20:43,400 --> 00:20:45,180
Kankichi-sensei, be careful!

357
00:20:50,860 --> 00:20:52,520
Everyone, hang in there!

358
00:20:52,820 --> 00:20:54,580
Mr. Kankitsu, do your best!

359
00:20:54,860 --> 00:20:56,500
Please take care of Kenta!

360
00:21:01,100 --> 00:21:03,200
Everyone, do your best!

361
00:21:07,180 --> 00:21:08,060
We're saved.

362
00:21:08,060 --> 00:21:11,460
Aaaah! Okay, extend the rope for me!

363
00:21:13,560 --> 00:21:15,540
One point turn, I'm coming now!

364
00:21:17,680 --> 00:21:18,560
Right?

365
00:21:24,860 --> 00:21:29,440
Each of you, Kenta found!
That's everyone found now!

366
00:21:33,420 --> 00:21:35,460
Okay, your feet are fine now.

367
00:21:36,020 --> 00:21:38,240
Listen, there's nothing to be scared of!

368
00:21:38,240 --> 00:21:40,300
Find your courage, all right?

369
00:21:40,300 --> 00:21:40,800
Yeah.

370
00:21:40,800 --> 00:21:42,660
Take a deep breath.

371
00:21:42,660 --> 00:21:43,480
Here I go!

372
00:21:53,220 --> 00:21:56,140
Yes! Okay! Pull me up!

373
00:21:59,320 --> 00:22:00,340
Kankichi-sensei!

374
00:22:02,880 --> 00:22:04,597
W-we dropped our phone,

375
00:22:04,647 --> 00:22:07,740
I thought no one could
hear my voice anymore.

376
00:22:08,020 --> 00:22:10,500
I thought no one would come to save us.

377
00:22:10,820 --> 00:22:12,340
I could hear you, you know.

378
00:22:12,520 --> 00:22:13,420
Kankichi-sensei!

379
00:22:13,900 --> 00:22:14,660
Kankichi-sensei!

380
00:22:14,980 --> 00:22:15,940
Kankichi-sensei!

381
00:22:17,020 --> 00:22:20,020
Look! There's such vast nature here.

382
00:22:20,380 --> 00:22:22,760
You kids shouldn't rely only on
phones and computers,

383
00:22:22,760 --> 00:22:24,920
you should make friends with nature more,

384
00:22:24,920 --> 00:22:27,620
and learn to have wild toughness too,

385
00:22:27,620 --> 00:22:29,880
or you won't survive in the world to come.

386
00:22:29,880 --> 00:22:30,900
Got it?

387
00:22:39,000 --> 00:22:41,040
So those are the kids from Shodoshima

388
00:22:41,520 --> 00:22:43,220
They all look healthy, don't they?

389
00:22:44,340 --> 00:22:46,940
This was taken on the day we said goodbye.

390
00:22:46,940 --> 00:22:49,460
At first, they were all like bean sprouts.

391
00:22:50,160 --> 00:22:52,740
So, Ryo-chan, what about the reward?

392
00:22:52,980 --> 00:22:53,680
Ta-da!

393
00:22:54,780 --> 00:22:57,900
Senpai, did you buy another new one?

394
00:22:58,160 --> 00:23:00,860
New models keep coming
out one after another.

395
00:23:01,340 --> 00:23:04,340
And with all sorts of things,
it's gone in no time.

396
00:23:04,340 --> 00:23:07,300
Sorry, Nakagawa,
could you lend me some money?

397
00:23:07,580 --> 00:23:10,240
Idiot, you went and wasted money again!

398
00:23:10,240 --> 00:23:11,325
Gah, Chief,

399
00:23:11,375 --> 00:23:14,780
No, this is, well, you see,
it's the information society.

400
00:23:14,780 --> 00:23:16,420
Hey, hey, Ryo-chan!

401
00:23:16,420 --> 00:23:18,940
Kankichi-sensei is getting scolded.

402
00:23:20,020 --> 00:23:21,540
We came on a social studies field trip.

403
00:23:21,540 --> 00:23:22,080
Hello.

404
00:23:22,760 --> 00:23:23,440
Everyone.

405
00:23:23,440 --> 00:23:26,460
Kankichi-sensei's phone!

406
00:23:26,460 --> 00:23:28,180
And it's the latest model, too!

407
00:23:29,960 --> 00:23:32,580
No, adults are allowed to use that one too.

408
00:23:33,360 --> 00:23:35,240
We have the same one too.

409
00:23:35,240 --> 00:23:35,940
What?

410
00:23:36,900 --> 00:23:38,860
We bought the computer in Akihabara too.

411
00:23:38,860 --> 00:23:41,580
We can't afford to fall behind the times,
you know.

412
00:23:42,060 --> 00:23:43,640
Senpai?

413
00:23:43,860 --> 00:23:45,260
That's not what you said.

414
00:23:45,260 --> 00:23:47,320
Well, even with all that nature around,

415
00:23:47,320 --> 00:23:48,850
but in the end, kids these days,

416
00:23:48,900 --> 00:23:52,220
I guess they really are
different from when we were young.

417
00:23:52,380 --> 00:23:57,160
Alright! Teacher Kankichi is going to show you Tokyo's hidden gems,
and I'll make sure you dig them all up!

418
00:23:57,540 --> 00:23:58,420
Yay!

419
00:23:58,900 --> 00:23:59,640
Let's go!

420
00:23:59,980 --> 00:24:01,260
Goo-bye!

421
00:24:17,320 --> 00:24:28,620
Even though he's a preschooler, why does he love period dramas?
Why is the Chief's little mustache so slightly small?

422
00:24:29,140 --> 00:24:36,480
Why is it?
Why does Honda-san's personality change when he rides a motorcycle?

423
00:24:36,480 --> 00:24:38,220
Why is it?

424
00:24:38,220 --> 00:24:42,260
The man who sleeps all day only
wakes up once every four years,

425
00:24:42,260 --> 00:24:43,400
why is that?

426
00:24:46,100 --> 00:24:52,560
Nakagawa-san won't lend money to Ryo-san,

427
00:24:53,320 --> 00:24:56,320
but he easily lends out
tanks and fighter jets.

428
00:24:56,320 --> 00:24:59,620
Why is it?

429
00:25:02,140 --> 00:25:06,940
Reiko-san is incredibly rich,

430
00:25:08,560 --> 00:25:12,500
yet why does she work at the police box?

431
00:25:13,240 --> 00:25:14,740
Why is it, I wonder?

432
00:25:14,740 --> 00:25:16,000
Why is it?

433
00:25:16,000 --> 00:25:17,240
Why is it?

434
00:25:17,240 --> 00:25:17,940
Why is it?

435
00:25:17,940 --> 00:25:18,640
Why is it?

436
00:25:18,640 --> 00:25:19,560
Why is that, I wonder?

437
00:25:29,540 --> 00:25:32,200
What? Me, chief of the Traffic Division?

438
00:25:32,440 --> 00:25:35,840
Promoted to sub-inspector,
leaping over Chief Ohara in rank.

439
00:25:35,840 --> 00:25:40,980
I see, I see. So the police finally
live in an age that values real ability.

440
00:25:40,980 --> 00:25:43,660
"Chief Ryotsu," what a lovely ring it has.

441
00:25:43,660 --> 00:25:47,440
Next time: Chief Kankichi Ryotsu,
so look forward to it!

442
00:25:59,620 --> 00:26:00,860
Thank you.

